<title>ESTONIA: EESTI KINDLUSTUS TO DECIDE ON SHARE ISSUE.</title>
<headline>EESTI KINDLUSTUS TO DECIDE ON SHARE ISSUE.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eesti Kindlustus, Estonia's largest insurance company, said on Wednesday that its shareholders will discuss profit distribution and a possible share issue on May 21.</p>
<p>Hoiupank has an 85 percent stake in the company and the rest is divided between Hansa Investments, the investment arm of Hansapank , Pindi Invest and Finland's Profit OY.</p>
<p>The shareholders will decide whether to issue new shares or offer existing shares via a tender, a spokesperson for the company told Reuters.</p>
<p>Eesti Kindlustus wants to list its shares on the Tallinn bourse, but at least 25 percent of a listed company's shares must be public.</p>
<p>The company earlier said that its board wants to retain its 1996 profit of 26 million kroons.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn Newsroom, +372 630 8400, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
</text>
